module examples.cost_itlb_span

# Cost-stage golden (plans/M20.md item M) — the **per-core I-TLB page
# span** (04 §5/§6, inventory row 16, `cost::footprint`).
#
# WHAT THIS PINS, PREDICTED FROM THE DOCS BEFORE THE CODE WAS RUN.
#
# `cost::footprint` computes a core's text span at the 4 KiB granule
# (`PAGE_BYTES`, the smallest the A76 TLBs support and therefore the one
# that spans the most pages — the over-cost direction) and charges one
# swept `tlb_walk_cost` per page beyond `[geometry] itlb_l1_entries =
# 48`, plus a second per page beyond `tlb_l2_entries = 1280`.
#
# The claim the term makes is that the denominator is **per core**
# (decision 1603): `PlacementTable::core_of` seals every actor to a
# core, a core's own methods count only for it, and only `Shared` text
# (runtime helpers, abort paths, free fns) counts for every core. This
# case is built to show exactly that asymmetry on one program:
#
#   * `Big` is sealed to **core 0** and carries its bulk as its own
#     methods, so that text lands on core 0 alone.
#   * `Small` is sealed to **core 1** and is tiny, so core 1's span is
#     essentially the shared runtime text.
#
# Predicted: two `Budget` lines on one program whose `text_pages` differ
# by an order of magnitude, core 0 over the 48-entry I-TLB with
# `over_itlb_pages = text_pages - 48` and a charge of one swept
# `tlb_walk_cost = 58` per page over, and `over_tlb_l2_pages = 0` (1280
# entries is 5 MiB away). No image-wide aggregate can state the first,
# which is decision 1603's whole point.
#
# The I-TLB budget breaks at 48 x 4096 = 196608 bytes of hot text on one
# core — three times the L1I cliff — which is why this case is bigger
# than `cost-icache-cliff` and why the two are separate cases.
#
# WHAT SHIPPING THIS CASE COSTS, RECORDED RATHER THAN AVOIDED
# (plans/M20.md decision 1635-M). `opts::win::itlb_absolute_breaches` /
# `VetoReason::ITlbBudgetExceeded` is an **absolute** veto, not a delta:
# a corpus case whose baseline is over the I-TLB refuses *every*
# candidate at *every* point of the residual box, the identity included.
# Measured: with this case at full size,
# `release_wins_at_every_point_of_the_residual_box` fails with
# `itlb_exceeded:cost-itlb-span:core0:57/48@…` at every point. That is
# exactly the failure decision 1619 describes for an absolute rule
# ("refuses a candidate for a property of the **baseline**"), and 1619
# kept the absolute I-side assertion only because item F had measured
# the span "inside budget on *both* surfaces". This case falsifies that
# premise. Retiring the absolute veto in favour of the delta rule that
# already covers `over_itlb_pages`, or excluding a deliberately-
# breaching case from `discover_cost_corpus`, is item J's surface — so
# the case ships and the refusal is left visible rather than a gate
# being weakened from a goldens item. On today's tree the refusal is not
# even reached: cases sweep in path order and `cost-crosscore` trips
# `MAX_SWEPT_DIMS` first (decision 1634-M).

